commit 288ce3e7ac0af0734567bd37e20101bb8b7f0430
Author: cqls <aaa@designconsultancy.co.uk>
Date:   Sat Aug 22 12:50:45 2026 +0100

    308 Phase A: CTA destination provenance is RECORDED, not derived - value-bound __cta_minted, both writers, register amended in the same commit

    Replaces LNK-033's derived provenance ('the resolver cannot produce a utility url, so a stored
    one was authored'), which bugs_open/308 cannot be fixed without falsifying. Owner-ruled
    2026-08-18: candidate 1, provenance first then the widening, no opt-out flags. Behaviour is
    unchanged until the candidate set widens - with no records in the DB and candidatesFromHubs
    still filtering, the resolver never mints a utility url so the new conjunct never fires.

    The signature is the enforcement: storedCTADestinationIsAuthored now takes (stored, field,
    validPages), so no caller can reach the utility-area shape test without the mint check. A call
    site holding only a url does not compile.

    VALUE-BOUND is the whole design. It makes 8 of RFC_042's 9 content_data writers correct with
    zero changes, and it is the only form that survives the section-editor MERGE: a presence-bound
    stamp would licence the recompute to clobber a human's edit, which is bugs_open/248 again.

    TWO DEFECTS FOUND DURING IMPLEMENTATION, both mine, both fixed here:
    - the persist merges SHALLOWLY and the record is a NESTED map, so a record for one slot
      REPLACED the stored record and dropped the sibling's - freezing it. Four of six ctaFieldNames
      components have two slots, so it is the common case. SeedCTAMinted fixes it, and it lives
      INSIDE both writers because a loop-level call was mutation-tested and proved DELETABLE with
      every test in the tree still green.
    - a second helper (CarryCTAMinted) for the unresolved fallthrough was written and then DELETED
      as redundant: mutation showed removing it changed no test, because the seed had already
      carried the record. Two guards in series with one dead is how an unexercised branch ships.

    Also corrected: I claimed NormalizePagePath equates /contact.html with /contact/index.html. It
    does NOT - it trims index.html and trailing slashes, so /contact/ and /contact/index.html both
    become /contact while /contact.html stays put. They are different pages here. The test caught
    it and now pins the boundary in both directions.

    NEITHER KEEP STAMPS, and both reasons are structural: reaching the 248 authored-utility keep
    PROVES the record does not cover the value, and the 299 non-page keep writes a URI REPAIR of an
    authored tel:/mailto:, so stamping it would make a phone button recomputable.

    Verified rather than assumed: the persist marshals the WHOLE map with no key filter
    (save_page_sections_action.go:968-1001), the envelope guard keys on the SIGNATURE not a key
    allow-list so it cannot refuse these saves, and 16 rows across four component functions already
    store an undeclared *_target_title. Mutation proofs run against a git archive HEAD scratch tree,
    because the working tree does not compile - another session's flag_page_image_rebuild_action.go
    is mid-edit.

    Register in the SAME commit per the ordering exemption's condition (2): LNK-035 added, LNK-033
    AMENDED visibly (its invariant is RETIRED by owner ruling, not quietly broken) with a correction
    to its own landmine, which listed 'widen the loaders' and 'drop candidatesFromHubs filter' as
    interchangeable when the loaders have a third consumer - the site header CTA fallback.

    Council round 1 REVISE read and acted on; round 2 resubmitted on the same correlation.

    Council-Submitted: e4336931-487b-4db3-b4dc-a4b128b3566c

